# A note that embeds a CSV file (![[Eruptions.csv]]) shows csv-table's preview of it in the
# reader, under the embed's name: csv-table (examples/extensions/csv-table, installed in the
# empty home by tests/drive.rs) answers file/preview with the file's first rows as a table. A
# change made to the CSV by another program brings a new preview. An embed of a file nobody
# owns (Kīlauea's picture) stays its name, as before.
size 120x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
write Inbox/Log.md # Log\n\nThe eruptions so far:\n\n![[Eruptions.csv]]\n\nAnd a picture: ![[kilauea-lava-lake.jpg]]\n
keys p
type log
wait-for Log
keys enter
wait-for Inbox/Log  reading
wait-for │ [[Krakatoa]]          1883    6
expect ⧉ Eruptions.csv
expect │ Volcano               Year    VEI    ›
expect And a picture: 🖼 kilauea-lava-lake.jpg
write Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv Volcano,Year,VEI,Notes\n[[Krakatoa]],1883,6,\n[[Tambora]],1815,7,\n
wait-for │ [[Tambora]]   1815    7
expect-not Vesuvius
screen
keys esc
wait-gone reading · Esc / q back
keys q
exits 0
